<title>USA: Southwestern Public sees Q2 charge.</title>
<headline>Southwestern Public sees Q2 charge.</headline>
<dateline>DALLAS 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Southwestern Public Service Co said on Monday that it is posting a $0.25 a share second quarter charge to write off its $16.1 million investment in the Carolina Energy Project in Kinston, N.C.</p>
<p>In February, Southwestern Public Service said the construction of the waste-to-energy project had been halted pending an independent analysis of the project's viability.</p>
<p>Banks that were providing debt financing to the project had withheld funds, Southwestern Public Service said in a statement.</p>
</text>
